<http://example.org/dengue/qa72> a ex:QA_Pair ;
    ex:answer_english "During the fever phase, the patient will have high fever for up to 2 to 7 days with red rash on the face and body, joint pain, muscle aches, headaches, pain behind the eye and sometimes other symptoms such as sore throat, red eyes, lack of appetite, nausea, vomiting and various sizes of skin (petechiae/ecchymosis," ;
